BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventdmvjazzseries3aalexhamburger26104-20261119@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261116T201549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:DMV Jazz Series: Alex Hamburger
DESCRIPTION:For the last decade\, flutist\, vocalist\, and composer Alex Hamburger has been creating her own musical direction. Her last album\, What If? \, delves into perception and the boundaries of human experience\, fusing electric and acoustic sounds and creating a stir with her band’s performances around the United States\, Europe\, and South America. Alex has been praised by publications around the globe as having the “ability to transform emotions into captivating melodies” that allow the listener “to be immersed within the blurred lines and the harmonious coexistence of light and dark that ultimately remind us all of the interconnectedness of our shared human experience.” Learn more about this show and Alex Hamburger by visiting her official website. This show is part of the DMV Jazz Series\, hosted by Eric Byrd and in partnership with the Frederick Jazz Society. New Spire Stages\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers an intimate venue for a memorable concert experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/dmv-jazz-series%3a-alex-hamburger/26104/
END:VEVENT
